     numbers; or, with -ss, only for special files and files with
     the set-user-id or set-group-id bit on).  By default,
     entries named .  and ..  are not printed; -aa prints them
     too.  Names ending in /.  identify directories.

     -aa   Include entries named .  and ..  in the output.

